NAME
  mount - mount a file system

SYNOPSIS
  mount
  mount LABEL PATH
  mount ADDRESS PATH

OPTIONS
  -r, --readonly  mount filesystem readonly
  -h, --help      print help message

DESCRIPTION
  Freax arranges mounted filesystems in one tree rooted at /. mount attaches
  an OC filesystem component; umount detaches it. Both require root.
  Bind mounts are not supported.

EXAMPLES
  mount
    Display a list of all currently mounted file systems.

  mount test /home
    Mounts the file system labeled `test` at `/home`.

  mount 56f /var
    Mounts the file system of which the address starts with `56f` at `/var`.

  mount --readonly tmpfs /tmp_ro
    Mounts a readonly access path of tmpfs to /tmp_ro
